## Blackwell × MacNeille × Le Cam
### Missing meets are nonprincipal cuts
Date: 2026-08-22
Status: EXACT ORDER-THEORETIC REFORMULATION; GENERIC ENGINE CLASSICAL

## 1. Autocorrection

The previous CW-001 continuation introduced a complete lattice of "coherent decision systems" in which the componentwise intersection

\[
C_k^\cap=\bigcap_p\mathcal R_k(\kappa_p)
\]

always exists.

That construction is valid, but it is not the smallest or most canonical order completion available.

Classical order theory already gives the exact minimal complete-lattice completion of any poset: the Dedekind–MacNeille completion.

Applying it to the Blackwell information poset produces a sharper statement.

The generic completion theorem is classical. The value here is the exact statistical interpretation of its cuts and their relation to reachable decision systems.

