# 7. Relation between the two completions

The earlier coherent-decision-system class is generally larger than the minimal MacNeille completion.

A MacNeille cut is always:

- downward closed in Blackwell order;
- closed under downstream post-processing;
- convex within a fixed output alphabet;
- arity-compatible;
- an intersection of principal reachable-decision systems.

Hence every MacNeille element has a coherent decision-system representation.

But an arbitrary coherent system need not satisfy the MacNeille closure condition

\[
A=L(U(A)).
\]

### Correction

The preferred canonical completion for pure order questions is therefore

\[
\boxed{
\operatorname{DM}(\mathsf B_X),
}
\]

not the full coherent-system lattice.

The coherent-system class remains useful as a concrete operational ambient space and as a possible domain for metrics/deficiencies.

